<title>GEORGIA: Georgia Jan-Oct trade deficit widens to $328.6 mln.</title>
<headline>Georgia Jan-Oct trade deficit widens to $328.6 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TBILISI 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's trade deficit widened to $328.6 million in the first 10 months of this year from a deficit of $129.5 million in the same period of 1995, the Department for Social and Economic Information said on Friday.</p>
<p>GEORGIA MERCHANDISE TRADE  Jan-Oct 96 Jan-Sept 96 Jan-Oct 95</p>
<p>    exports	 ($ million)	  152.3	135.5	 116.6</p>
<p>    imports			    480.9	438.2	 246.2</p>
<p>    trade balance		   -328.6     -302.7	-129.5</p>
<p>(differences due to rounding)</p>
<p>The deficit with countries excluding the former Soviet Union was $243.4 million.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
